00:33:52,260 --> 00:33:56,780
Just to make sure that, just so you guys can know that I'm not making stuff up.

552
00:33:56,780 --> 00:33:57,760
Okay?

553
00:33:58,620 --> 00:34:01,480
Deuteronomy chapter 7, verse 6 through 8.

554
00:34:01,480 --> 00:34:03,900
This is what the Lord said to Israel.

555
00:34:03,900 --> 00:34:06,800
Deuteronomy is a very important book for the people of Israel.

556
00:34:06,800 --> 00:34:07,280
Right?

557
00:34:07,280 --> 00:34:08,640
It's really sealing a covenant.

558
00:34:08,640 --> 00:34:09,700
And this is what he says.

559
00:34:10,040 --> 00:34:13,960
For you are a holy people belonging to the Lord, your God.

560
00:34:13,960 --> 00:34:19,680
The Lord, your God, has chosen you to be his own possession out of all the peoples of the face of the earth.

561
00:34:19,680 --> 00:34:31,100
And the Lord has had his heart set on you and chose you, not because you were more numerous than all peoples, for you were, like, the fewest of all peoples.

562
00:34:31,320 --> 00:34:41,800
But because the Lord loved you and kept the oath, he swore to your ancestors, he brought you out with a strong hand and redeemed you.

563
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:48,740
That means he bought you back from a place of slavery and from the power of the Pharaoh, king of Egypt.

564
00:34:48,740 --> 00:34:52,820
So this is what the whole nation of Israel is being told.

565
00:34:52,820 --> 00:34:54,060
You think you're worthy?

566
00:34:54,060 --> 00:34:55,640
Like, you are so not worthy.

567
00:34:55,640 --> 00:34:57,400
It's just because God loves you.

568
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:58,620
And that's better.

569
00:35:01,320 --> 00:35:01,720
Right?

570
00:35:01,720 --> 00:35:07,800
Like, think about what I did for my kids.

571
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:10,840
Right?

572
00:35:10,840 --> 00:35:13,340
My wife and I, we bring them home from the hospital.

573
00:35:13,340 --> 00:35:15,800
Whose name do they carry?

574
00:35:15,800 --> 00:35:17,040
Mine.

575
00:35:17,040 --> 00:35:20,220
Whose house do they live in?

576
00:35:20,220 --> 00:35:21,120
Mine.

577
00:35:21,120 --> 00:35:22,700
Whose food do they eat?

578
00:35:22,700 --> 00:35:23,400
Mine.

579
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:26,000
Why?

580
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:26,840
Because they're worthy?

581
00:35:26,840 --> 00:35:28,740
No, it's because I set my heart on you.

582
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:35,020
And so I give you identity and position and place and security.

583
00:35:35,020 --> 00:35:35,560
Right?

584
00:35:35,560 --> 00:35:41,980
This is reiterated to the New Testament church in Tigat chapter 2, verse 14.

585
00:35:41,980 --> 00:35:43,120
I love this language.

586
00:35:43,120 --> 00:35:43,600
It says,

587
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:54,820
He gave himself for us to redeem us from all lawlessness and to cleanse for himself.

588
00:35:54,880 --> 00:35:57,780
You see that redeeming and cleansing language, right?

589
00:35:57,780 --> 00:36:00,760
It implies you're not like that worthy.

590
00:36:00,760 --> 00:36:04,360
Like, you were a criminal and dirty.

591
00:36:06,820 --> 00:36:18,320
And he gave himself for you to redeem you and to cleanse, I love this language, cleanse for himself a people for his own possession.

592
00:36:18,320 --> 00:36:21,640
Eager to do good works.

593
00:36:21,640 --> 00:36:24,280
Guys, when you think about it, listen, right?

594
00:36:24,320 --> 00:36:27,640
We want to keep it moderated because obviously there's some relationships that are unhealthy and controlling.

595
00:36:27,640 --> 00:36:29,020
But hear me out on this.

596
00:36:29,020 --> 00:36:33,760
Have you really thought about the fact that the language of love is a possessive language?

597
00:36:33,760 --> 00:36:36,440
Right?

598
00:36:38,720 --> 00:36:46,180
When you really love someone, there's a healthy degree of possessiveness that comes with that.

599
00:36:46,180 --> 00:36:47,760
Right?

600
00:36:49,200 --> 00:36:50,980
Andrea is not a wife.

601
00:36:50,980 --> 00:36:52,440
She is my wife.

602
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:54,140
Right?

603
00:36:54,140 --> 00:36:55,780
That's not a baby.

604
00:36:55,780 --> 00:36:57,140
That's my baby.

605
00:36:57,140 --> 00:36:59,040
It's my son.

606
00:36:59,040 --> 00:37:02,360
We use possessive language in love all the time.

607
00:37:02,360 --> 00:37:10,880
And I love this language where, like, I read that and I'm like, oh, man, I want to be God's possession.

608
00:37:10,880 --> 00:37:13,980
I know what that means.

609
00:37:14,640 --> 00:37:18,920
I know what it meant when I took the baby home and said, you're my son.

610
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:20,360
I want that.

611
00:37:20,360 --> 00:37:20,820
Oh, yeah.

612
00:37:20,820 --> 00:37:22,800
Like, take me home, God.

613
00:37:22,800 --> 00:37:23,240
Right?

614
00:37:23,240 --> 00:37:24,320
Okay.

615
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:27,220
But neither son understood this.

616
00:37:27,220 --> 00:37:30,960
They both thought it had something to do with their worth.

617
00:37:30,960 --> 00:37:37,960
The father's love, therefore, is actually the most valuable thing that the son's possessed.

618
00:37:37,960 --> 00:37:41,520
His love established who they were.

619
00:37:41,520 --> 00:37:44,520
Right?

620
00:37:45,460 --> 00:37:47,440
His love established who they were.

621
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:51,720
This is the father's role in their life, to give them an identity, like a place.

